window.docContents[29].resolve({"/Design-restrictions/Polymorphism/#Core-C______--Design-restrictions--Polymorphism":{"contents":"C++17 has function templates, class templates with several parameters, partial specialisation and the ranking of implicit conversion sequences in overload resolution (N4659 §16.3.3.2). The call g(true) with the overloads g(int) and g(long) selects g(int) in g++, by the promotion of bool.Core C++ admits class templates with one type parameter, instantiated in type position, . Overloading selects by argument type without a ranking, . The keyword auto declares local variables only, .The restriction expands every template before the type check, , so the type checker and the evaluator see only classes. The choice of an overload has three outcomes, the one candidate that accepts the arguments, an exact candidate among several, or an error.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Design restrictions","header":"9.5. Polymorphism","id":"/Design-restrictions/Polymorphism/#Core-C______--Design-restrictions--Polymorphism"},"/Storage-and-commands/Rules-of-the-chapter/#Core-C______--Storage-and-commands--Rules-of-the-chapter":{"contents":"Every typing rule and every evaluation rule of this chapter, in the order of its sections, the typing rules of each section before its evaluation rules. The section named above each rule states it with its explanation and with the definition of its notation.\n\nDeclaration\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nLocal reference\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nAssignment\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nSequence and block\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nConditional\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nLoops\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nExpression statement\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Storage and commands","header":"4.9. Rules of the chapter","id":"/Storage-and-commands/Rules-of-the-chapter/#Core-C______--Storage-and-commands--Rules-of-the-chapter"}});